·  \mathcal{E}_{\text{dist}} : same structure as  \mathcal{E}_{\text{base}} , with shifted frequencies, amplitudes, and noise realizations.
·  \mathcal{E}_{\text{sem}} :  A  has energy in  [20,50]  Hz without  f_\star ;  B  has energy in  [200,500]  Hz without  f_\star ;  C  is  f_\star = 100  Hz alone.

In  \mathcal{E}_{\text{base}}  and  \mathcal{E}_{\text{dist}} ,  f_\star  is present in both  A  and  B  and is non-discriminative. In  \mathcal{E}_{\text{sem}} ,  f_\star  is the sole predictor of  C . This resolves the inconsistency:  A  and  B  are not unchanged in  \mathcal{E}_{\text{sem}}  with respect to  f_\star ; they lose it.

C.2 Filter Bank Implementation

· Order  n = 4 .
· Number of filters  m = 32 .
· Center frequencies  f_i  log-spaced in  [20,1000]  Hz.
· Bandwidth  b_i = 1.019 \cdot \operatorname{ERB}(f_i) .
· Temporal-integration constant  \tau_i = k/f_i  with  k = 3 .
· Envelope via the leaky integrator in Appendix A.2.
· Inactive slots (after distillation) are set to zero in  \Phi_G .

C.3 Controller Architecture

· Hidden dimension  d_h = 64 .
· Input dimension  m = 32 .
· Output dimension  |\mathcal{Y}| = 4 .
· Input layer: 1-D convolution along channel axis with fixed random kernel  W_{\text{conv}}  of width  w = 5 .
·  W_{zh} \in \mathbb{R}^{64 \times 32}  initialized from  \mathcal{U}(-1/\sqrt{32}, 1/\sqrt{32}) .

C.4 Training Protocol

· Optimizer: Adam with learning rate  10^{-3} .
· Batch size: 32.
· Training budget  B : 5000 episodes.
· Early stopping: validation loss with patience 500.
· Selection set  \mathcal{D}_{\text{sel}} : 500 fresh samples from the parent’s environment (not the current environment), to eliminate generational data leakage.
· Test set  \mathcal{D}_{\text{test}} : 1000 samples from the current environment.

C.5 Distillation Parameters

· Supervised distillation threshold  \varepsilon = 0.05 .
· Perceptual distillation target size  m' = 16 .
· Mutation standard deviation  \sigma = 0.1 .

