Appendix E — Statistical Analysis Plan

E.1 Primary Comparison

The pre-registered primary comparison is  P_{\text{Per}}  vs  D  on  N^\star_{85}  in Phase 3.  N^\star_{85}  is the number of training episodes required to reach  85\%  balanced accuracy on  \mathcal{E}_{\text{sem}} .

E.2 Secondary Comparisons

Five pairwise comparisons with Holm correction:

1.  P_{\text{Per}}  vs  D 
2.  P_{\text{Per}}  vs  P_{\text{Sup}} 
3.  P_{\text{Per}}  vs  P_R 
4.  P_{\text{Per}}  vs  P_S 
5.  P_{\text{Sup}}  vs  D 

Holm is uniformly more powerful than Bonferroni and controls family-wise error without unnecessary conservatism.

E.3 Power Analysis

With  n = 10  paired observations, the Wilcoxon signed-rank test at  \alpha = 0.01  and  r_{rb} = 0.5  has approximately  10\%  power. To achieve  80\%  power for  r_{rb} = 0.5 , approximately  n \approx 55  seeds are required. To achieve  80\%  power for  r_{rb} = 0.9 ,  n = 10  is sufficient.

E.4 Censoring

 N^\star_{85}  is right-censored: some runs may not reach  85\%  accuracy within budget  B . Treat  N^\star_{85}  as a censored survival time and use a log-rank test or Cox proportional hazards model with group as the covariate. Report the censoring rate per group. If censoring exceeds  20\% , the primary analysis is the survival model, not the Wilcoxon test.

E.5 Effect Size

Matched-pairs rank-biserial correlation  r_{rb} . Interpretation:  |r_{rb}| \approx 0.1  (small),  \approx 0.3  (moderate),  \ge 0.5  (large).


